# Recon Studio — per-machine config for run.sh. Copy to `local.env` and edit (gitignored).
# All values are optional — run.sh auto-detects sensible defaults when unset.
# Note: storage/browse vars use the RECON_STUDIO_ prefix; the tuning vars (MAX_JOBS /
# RESIZE_WORKERS / BACKENDS) still keep the COLMAP_PANEL_ prefix for back-compat.
# run.sh loads this file with `set -a`, so every var here is exported into the server
# AND inherited by the tools it shells out to (ffmpeg / colmap / gsutil).

# --- binaries (PATH by default; set only for non-standard installs) ---
# COLMAP_BIN=colmap                          # e.g. /opt/colmap/bin/colmap
# FFMPEG_BIN=/mnt/ssd1/bin/ffmpeg-nvdec      # ffmpeg with blurdetect (+ NVDEC for GPU decode)
# FFMPEG_HWACCEL=cuda                        # set to "none" to force CPU decode

# --- conda env ---
# CONDA_ROOT=/home/aibox/miniconda3          # auto-detected via `conda info --base` if unset
# CONDA_ENV=rec                              # the panel's own (torch-free) env (default: rec)

# --- training backends ---
# The trainers (gs2m, …) run in their OWN conda envs as subprocesses — the panel
# never imports torch. Built-in defaults assume sibling envs ($CONDA_ROOT/envs/gs2m)
# and sibling repos (../GS-2M). To override per machine, copy backends.example.json
# to backends.json. Run /doctor to verify each backend's env + CUDA before training.
# COLMAP_PANEL_BACKENDS=/path/to/backends.json   # default: ./backends.json
#
# Compiled backends (e.g. LichtFeld Studio — "launch":"binary" + "exec" in backends.json)
# run a built executable instead of a conda env (training only, no mesh; 去背 still works
# → downloads a cleaned cloud). The subprocess inherits the panel's environment, so if the
# binary can't find its shared libs when launched from the panel, set LD_LIBRARY_PATH here:
# LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/home/will/repo/LichtFeld-Studio/build:/usr/local/cuda/lib64

# --- depth/normal maps (LichtFeld-Studio `preprocess`) ---
# The 🌊 深度 tool now runs LichtFeld-Studio's own `preprocess` subcommand (the
# same compiled binary the lichtfeld-* trainers use — MoGe-2 ONNX, self-
# downloading, no conda env / torch needed). It writes `depth/` and/or
# `normals/` next to `images/`, which `--use-depth-loss` / `--use-normal-loss`
# discover automatically. No config needed here — see the lichtfeld-mrnf
# backend's "exec" path (backends.py) for where the binary is expected.

# --- storage / browsing (local) ---
# Unset, run.sh auto-picks the roomiest local NON-ROOT mount (root is excluded on
# purpose: it's the OS disk, and a COLMAP/training run that fills it takes the whole
# machine down). Set these only to override that choice.
# DATA_DISK_MIN_GB=50                             # smallest mount run.sh will consider
# RECON_STUDIO_DATA=/mnt/ssd1/recon_studio/data   # job state + logs (use a roomy disk)
# RECON_STUDIO_BROWSE_ROOT=/mnt/ssd1              # directory-picker root (local file browser)
# TMPDIR=/mnt/ssd1/recon_studio/data/tmp          # ffmpeg/colmap scratch

# --- GCS browse + download (gsutil) ---
# The GCS tab shells out to `gsutil` (Google Cloud SDK; must be installed + authed via
# `gcloud auth login`). It only moves bytes gs:// -> local; the pipeline never reads a
# bucket directly.
# GSUTIL_BIN=gsutil                               # PATH by default; set for non-standard installs
# CLOUDSDK_CORE_PROJECT=my-gcp-project            # default GCP project for gsutil. REQUIRED to
#                                                 # browse from the bucket list: `gsutil ls` with no
#                                                 # arg needs a project id, else it errors out.
# RECON_STUDIO_GCS_ROOT=gs://my-bucket/datasets/  # start the GCS browser here (empty = list all buckets)
# RECON_STUDIO_DEST_ROOT=/mnt/ssd1                # local root that GCS downloads land under (default: /)

# --- concurrency ---
# How many jobs may run at the same time (抽幀/COLMAP/訓練/Mesh 共用此上限)。
# GPU 仍由各任務的 GPU 欄位手動指定;此數字不會自動分配顯卡。
# COLMAP_PANEL_MAX_JOBS=4
# COLMAP 的 FullHD resize 平行 ffmpeg worker 數(預設 = CPU 核數,上限 32)。
# COLMAP_PANEL_RESIZE_WORKERS=24

# --- server ---
# 面板綁在哪。預設只收本機,因為面板本身沒有任何登入機制,又能瀏覽
# RECON_STUDIO_BROWSE_ROOT 底下的檔案、還會開子行程。
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8077
#
# 要讓同事連得到,不要改成 0.0.0.0,跑:
#   sudo scripts/deploy-nginx-lan.sh
#
# 同事看到的網址。預設 recon.venraas.tw —— 用專案自己的名字,不要借別的服務的
# (claude.venraas.tw 是同一台機器上的 LLM 聊天站)。這個名字要有一筆 A 記錄指到
# 本機區網 IP;還沒加之前 https://<區網IP>:8443/ 一樣可以用,腳本會把該下的
# gcloud 指令印出來。
# RECON_STUDIO_LAN_DOMAIN=recon.venraas.tw
# 它把面板放到 nginx 後面(固定網址 + TLS + 帳密),面板本身維持 127.0.0.1,
# 而且網址不會因為你關掉 VS Code / 斷線就失效。裝好之後 ./run.sh 會把網址印出來,
# ./run.sh --doctor 的「區網代理 (nginx)」會檢查它有沒有跟 PORT 對得上。
#
# 這兩個名字跟外界撞名(conda 的編譯器會 export HOST=x86_64-conda-linux-gnu,
# 很多工具會 export PORT),所以 run.sh 只認 local.env 裡的 HOST/PORT;
# 要從環境變數一次性覆蓋,用不會撞名的這組:
# RECON_STUDIO_HOST=0.0.0.0
# RECON_STUDIO_PORT=8077

# --- SuperSplat(去背編輯器 / 點雲 viewer)---
# run.sh 啟動時自動同步到最新 upstream release(背景跑、原子換版、失敗沿用現有版本)。
# 關掉自動更新:
# SUPERSPLAT_AUTOUPDATE=0
# 釘住特定版本(配合 AUTOUPDATE=1 會在啟動時確保就是這版):
# SUPERSPLAT_VER=v2.27.4
